Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["The Circuit-Level Layer, Function by Function", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The companion note ",
 StyleBox["Stabilizer Codes in the Quantum Framework", "TI"],
 " reads the code layer from the outside: codes in, error rates out. This one \
opens it. It walks the four modules that turn a code into a noisy experiment \
\[LongDash] ",
 Cell["Circuit.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 ", ",
 Cell["DetectorModel.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 ", ",
 Cell["Memory.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " and ",
 Cell["Stim.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " \[LongDash] and calls ",
 StyleBox["every",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " function in them on a real code, including the ones that are internal to \
the package."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reason to document internals at all is that they are where the physics \
is. A syndrome is a matrix product only as long as the measurement is assumed \
perfect; once a check is a subcircuit, a fault in it can spread, and the \
object that records how is the detector error model. Reading the layer from \
the outside you see a polynomial in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 "; reading it from the inside you see why that polynomial has a linear \
term."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["The chain each section follows:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
    QECCode  ->  instructions + Pauli frame       (Circuit.wl)              \
->  fault -> detectors, observables  (DetectorModel.wl)              ->  \
decode, and a rate               (Memory.wl)              ->  the same \
experiment in Stim      (Stim.wl)\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["Loading the layer", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The code layer is a development package under ",
 Cell["OngoingProjects/QEC/", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ", so this page loads both the framework and the layer itself, exactly as \
the companion note does. Symbols introduced here stay bound for the whole \
page:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

