Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Idle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["modelled",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] see the schedule above \[LongDash] but it still ",
 StyleBox["defaults to zero",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and that default is optimistic rather than neutral. The generators are \
extracted one after another rather than interleaved, so there is ",
 StyleBox["more", "TI"],
 " waiting, not less. What excuses it is that a fixed-size code extracted \
serially is a constant number of steps \[LongDash] not the claim that there \
is no time step to idle in, which section 15.5.2 of the book explicitly \
forbids."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell["DetectorModel.wl \[LongDash] from faults to detectors", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Once the checks are measured by a circuit, a syndrome bit is no longer \
trustworthy on its own: it can be wrong because the data was hit or because \
the readout lied, and one round cannot tell those apart. The fix used here is \
to decode the ",
 StyleBox["differences", "TI"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], "1"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "1"], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "final"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell["\<\
A detector is a parity that is deterministically 0 when nothing goes wrong, \
so a fired detector is unambiguous evidence of a fault, and a readout error \
fires two detectors in a row rather than looking like a data error.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Whose fix this is matters. The book's answer to an untrustworthy syndrome \
is repeat ",
 StyleBox["and agree", "TI"],
 ": trust a run of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " consecutive identical syndromes. Differencing consecutive syndromes and \
decoding the whole spacetime history is a different procedure, from the \
topological-code literature \[LongDash] Dennis, Kitaev, Landahl and Preskill \
\[LongDash] and as an explicit object with an error model attached it is \
Gidney's Stim. Section 12.2.2 of the book raises the strategy and declines to \
analyse it: ",
 StyleBox["\"it is difficult to analyze such strategies in the completely \
general case.\"", "TI"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell["The default number of rounds", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bfData", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"codeData", "[", "bitFlip", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"defaultRounds", "[", "bfData", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"defaultRounds", "[", 
    RowBox[{"codeData", "[", "five", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"roundLength", "[", 
    RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "3", ",", "8"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[38]= ",ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default is the code distance, which is the topological-memory \
convention: with repeated noisy measurement the history is a lattice in one \
more dimension, and taking fewer rounds than the distance protects the time \
direction less than the space ones. It is deliberately ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " the book's fault-tolerant criterion, and the two should not be conflated."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell["The mechanism list", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A mechanism is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<Faults\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"index", ",", " ", "qubit", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], 
      "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Location\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "label"}]}], "|>"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Location\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " is the key to everything downstream: it groups mechanisms that are \
alternatives of the same physical location."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mechC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"faultMechanisms", "[", 
    RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"First", "[", 
      RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "mechC", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "[", "mechC", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"64", ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"Faults\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "4", ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"Probability\"\>", "\[Rule]", "p"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"Location\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\<\"Reset\"\>", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[39]= ",ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three per one-qubit gate at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 ", fifteen per CNOT at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "15"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 ", one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],
 " before each measurement, one after each reset:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Counts", "[", 
  RowBox[{"First", " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
    RowBox[{"mechC", ",", " ", "\"\<Location\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"Reset\"\>", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"TwoQubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "60"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Measurement\"\>", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[40]= ",ExpressionUUID->"604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Waiting is the fifth kind, and it is the one that only appears if you ask \
for it. The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Idle\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 " rate defaults to zero, and at zero ",
 Cell[BoxData["idleMechanisms"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 " returns nothing at all rather than a list of zero-probability rows \
\[LongDash] so every number in this note is what it was before the schedule \
existed. Turn it on and three Paulis appear per idle slot:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"idleMech", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"sym", "[", "\"\<idleMechanisms\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"withIdle", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<OneQubit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<TwoQubit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Measurement\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Reset\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Idle\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "pIdle"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "mechC", "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
    RowBox[{"faultMechanisms", "[", 
     RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "[", "withIdle", "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
   ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"3", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
     RowBox[{"circuitIdleSlots", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"codeCircInstr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], "\n", "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"64", ",", "118", ",", "54"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[41]= ",ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bit-flip extraction circuit has no one-qubit gates at all \[LongDash] \
both checks are pure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],
 ", so nothing needs rotating \[LongDash] which makes it a clean place to see \
the idle count on its own."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell["\<\
Phenomenological instead puts three Paulis on each data qubit at the start of \
each round, plus one flip per readout:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mechP", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"faultMechanisms", "[", 
    RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"First", "[", 
      RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<BitFlip\>\"", ",", " ", "p", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<MeasurementError\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "q"}]}], "]"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "mechP", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Counts", "[", 
    RowBox[{"First", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
      RowBox[{"mechP", ",", " ", "\"\<Location\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"11", ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"Data\"\>", "\[Rule]", "9"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"Measurement\"\>", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], 
    "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[42]= ",ExpressionUUID->"4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The book counts the identity as an admissible outcome at a faulty location; \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "15"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 " here exclude it, which makes this marginally ",
 StyleBox["less", "TI"],
 " conservative. And listing the three outcomes of a depolarizing channel as \
three independent mechanisms is an approximation \[LongDash] the same one \
Stim makes. Sampling draws the true channel, so simulated numbers are exact; \
only the probabilities attached to the rows are approximate, and the \
minimum-weight decoder does not read them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell["What one fault does", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["faultEffect"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 " runs the frame propagator and reads the residual through the code's label \
matrix. One GF(2) matrix product returns both halves: the syndrome a perfect \
final round would see, and the logical class."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bfInstr", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"codeCircInstr", "[", 
    RowBox[{"bfData", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"faultEffect", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "bfData", ",", " ", "bfInstr", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1", 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[43]= ",ExpressionUUID->"5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 " on data qubit 1 fires the checks it anticommutes with, and flips nothing \
logical."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],
 " on the same qubit. It is invisible to a bit-flip code's checks \[LongDash] \
but it ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " a logical:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"faultEffect", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "bfData", ",", " ", "bfInstr", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1", 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[44]= ",ExpressionUUID->"04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
No detector, one observable. A weight-one undetectable fault, which is the \
distance-1 result from the top of the page seen from inside the circuit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["recordDetectors"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],
 " is the piece that turns a raw measurement record into that detector \
vector. Given two rounds of two checks plus the final syndrome:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"recordDetectors", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[45]= ",ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"]
}, Open  ]],

